WEBVTT

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:08.400
As we cast our eyes above to the boundless sky, we know

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:16.450
Whatever tomorrow brings, the sun will always shine

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.540
So won't you come with me?

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:37.600
It's almost time for the school bell to ring

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:39.810
And every moment by moment

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:42.230
I feel more and more like I could fly

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:45.690
This feeling fills my thoughts and sets my heart alight

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:49.150
It's this moment I love most of all

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:53.820
In my bag I hold all the things I've overcome

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:57.580
And on their wings, I'll fly into the future

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:02.080
We can do anything, at any time and any place

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:05.590
And no one can stop us even if they try

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:10.220
From ING and that alone can we proceed

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:14.140
Carrying all our feelings as we go

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:18.140
Flying with our dreams for all to see

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:24.610
Let's close today's chapter, and start a new page!

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:35.490
Broken

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:39.540
So I've got a question...

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:41.250
What is it, Sixteen-chan?

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:43.580
If he's so clueless, why did he come here?

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.380
You mean our teacher?

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:49.000
Who else would I be talking about?

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.130
Yeah.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:52.720
I think he's trying hard, though.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:55.140
He's doing his best to understand more about us.

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:01.270
Have you thought about

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:05.310
the person who's going to end up holding you?

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:08.610
Well, yeah, of course. A little.

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:11.240
But what does that have to do with our Japanese teacher?

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:14.910
Well, it's not really about him specifically,

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:20.830
but I ran into him during the summer festival, just before he came to our school.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:26.380
I never knew you met him before.

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:28.960
He had a great stance with a gun,

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:32.510
and I started thinking that if someone held me like that...

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:42.810
<i>My hammer... My hammer's going to fire...</i>

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:48.900
Funko's a perv.

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:51.530
That's not what I meant!

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:13.630
How lon' you gonn' be wor'ing on that?

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:16.930
Well, I can't decide what to write.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:19.010
Just put down something random.

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:20.390
Take a look at mine.

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:26.440
That's all?

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:27.770
It's enough.

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:28.650
What does everyone else's say?

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.820
<i>Maybe I'm thinking too hard about this.</i>

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:43.200
Sig-chan! Here I come!

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:45.580
Yippee!

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:52.380
That hurt, Funko-chan!

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:54.590
Sorry.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:02.470
Sure is cold.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:09.850
Here you go.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.310
So warm!

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:23.120
Um...

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:28.960
Sig-chan?

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:35.840
They're having fun out there, even though it's so cold.

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:37.630
I wouldn't be able to stand that weather.

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:48.680
It's ready?

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:49.640
Yeah!

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:53.980
Hey, the rice cakes are ready.

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:55.730
Don't stay cooped up in there!

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:58.400
Get out here and come sledding with us!

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.400
I don't like the cold!

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:02.360
You're no fun.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:04.320
I'm plenty fun!

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:05.780
It's cold just sitting here!

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:08.250
Why would I want to freeze my face off riding a sled?!

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:09.960
How about this then?

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:17.380
What are you doing?

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:19.300
It's done!

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:20.630
What's that?

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:22.380
It's a snow angel.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.760
Doesn't it look like an angel to you?

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:27.220
People in Europe do this a lot.

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:30.810
Sig-chan's is better!

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:32.810
Mine are pieces of art.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:38.070
That's terrible!

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:41.360
Do people in cold places find stuff like that fun?

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:42.030
That was mean!

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:48.990
What are you doing, Sig?

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:51.830
I guess the three-round burst is pretty weak after all.

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.670
Letting a little cold weather beat you.

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:57.380
Sounds like you're just complaining 'cause you're weaker.

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:58.710
What was that?!

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:00.510
S-Sig-chan...

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:05.300
Normally I'd make you pay for that comment,

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:07.430
but you're not gonna lure me outside that easily.

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:09.970
You just want to get me angry and goad me into a snowball fight, don't you?

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:12.430
Then I'll give you a handicap.

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:15.980
You'll be with Elle, and she's awful at long range.

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:18.980
It wouldn't be fair otherwise.

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:20.780
Right?

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:26.240
It's pretty cold.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.790
You look like you're enjoying it.

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:32.290
Bring it on!

00:06:32.290 --> 00:06:34.290
You're pretty simple, aren't you, Sixteen?!

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:36.710
Calm down, you two!

00:06:36.710 --> 00:06:36.960
Take this!

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:38.380
They sure are energetic.
Take this!

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:38.920
They sure are energetic.

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:41.300
Oh, it's our teacher.

00:06:42.010 --> 00:06:44.340
Sensei, you wanna play too?

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:47.340
As usual, you just love spraying bullets.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:48.350
Shut up!

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:50.140
You got that?

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:51.720
First one to give up is the loser.

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:53.640
Make whatever rules you want.

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:54.600
I'll roll with it.

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:59.190
Sink into a sea of snow!

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:01.820
Here.

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:03.360
Here.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:06.950
We make a good team.

00:07:07.450 --> 00:07:09.530
Hey, what exactly is my role here?

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:11.620
Hurry up and make more ammo.

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:14.410
If you don't get to it, I'll turn into a semi-auto.

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:29.890
Of all the places for an obstacle to pop up!

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:31.600
Hey...

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:36.180
You're the perfect teacher, risking yourself to protect a student.

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:40.810
Yay!

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:41.770
We did it!

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:55.500
Payback!

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:59.000
What are you doing to Funko-chan?

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:06.010
Now you've done it!

00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:12.300
What's that sound?

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:13.760
It's coming from up there.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:19.230
Elle! Stop! Stop!

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:26.780
This is bad.

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:29.530
I can't feel my fingertips anymore.

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:34.870
This is supposed to be warm, but it doesn't feel warm at all.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.460
This can't be good...

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:45.670
I'm starting to space out...

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:48.590
I should eat something to regain my strength.

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:51.800
I don't have enough energy to make anything.

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:52.890
Yeah.

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:56.310
I could make something for you guys if you want.

00:08:56.310 --> 00:08:57.970
Thank you.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:08:59.850
Wait, why are you fine?

00:09:00.230 --> 00:09:05.520
I was designed to be able to fire even when covered in ice in temperatures of -20° C.

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:07.320
Minus 20?!

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:18.910
You can't have a Swiss assault rifle that can't fire from the top of Jungfrau.

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:24.290
Switzerland's amazing!

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:30.010
Are these Eighteen-chan's rice cakes?

00:09:30.010 --> 00:09:33.050
Yeah, she was born here in Japan,

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:35.930
so her mom sends them over.

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:38.850
Why are they at Sixteen-chan's place?

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:40.560
I'm home!

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:43.060
Speak of the devil.

00:09:44.690 --> 00:09:46.520
Eighteen-chan, over here!

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:48.820
We're having a hotpot party.

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:50.110
Oh, here's a gift for you.

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:53.030
Um... Thanks.

00:09:59.040 --> 00:09:59.700
Huh?

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:01.960
Where are the vegetables?

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:03.040
There aren't any.

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:05.130
I... see.

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:08.210
Sig, what's this?

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:10.460
It's the Belgian flag.

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:11.420
Nice, huh?

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:15.010
Tomatoes, cheese, and for Funko, Belgian chocolate.

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:16.970
Thank you, Sig-chan!

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:20.720
Who put Sig in charge of the food?!

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:32.690
Oh yeah, I heard from Fourteen-onee

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:36.740
that our Japanese teacher was wearing this huge mask,

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:39.780
and buying tons of instant noodles.

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:41.790
It must be awful living alone.

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:43.750
I wonder if he caught a cold.

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:46.960
Maybe that snowball fight did him in...

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:52.590
It must be tough being human.

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:53.800
Yeah!

00:10:55.510 --> 00:10:56.630
Oh, that's it!

00:10:57.470 --> 00:11:00.100
How about we all pay him a visit?

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:01.510
We can go make sure he's all right!

00:11:01.850 --> 00:11:03.680
Huh, that's surprising.

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:06.190
I wouldn't have expected you to say that.

00:11:06.190 --> 00:11:07.060
Really?

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:10.520
<i>I found a way to kill time.</i>

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:16.570
Oh yeah, what was his name again?

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:18.700
Isn't his name Japanese Teacher?

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:19.950
Yeah, it's Japanese Teacher.

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:21.370
Japanese Teacher.

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:29.380
It's so cold...

00:11:33.090 --> 00:11:35.130
Well, where does he live?

00:11:36.510 --> 00:11:39.340
He lives right behind our dorm.

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:41.720
Lighthouse motocross?

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:43.680
Sixteen-chan, that's...

00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:01.450
We can't really go there empty-handed, though.

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:03.030
You're right.

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:04.160
Let's go buy something.

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:06.750
How much should we all chip in?

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:10.380
About 200 yen each should be good.

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:11.670
Seems about right.

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:12.670
Yeah.

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:15.210
Huh? Where's Elle-chan?

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:18.090
That broken girl...

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:21.090
Now's the only time she's actually good at running away.

00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:34.690
Come on, Sixteen-chan.

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:36.860
Don't just put in cans of peaches.

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:39.150
Then, how about tangerines?

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:39.780
Honestly...

00:12:40.240 --> 00:12:42.120
They're the thing to eat when you're sick!

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:47.540
Fukko!

00:12:47.540 --> 00:12:48.580
Fukko, look over here!

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:49.330
What is it?

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:51.580
I've got dog ears.

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:54.170
Stop messing around.

00:12:54.170 --> 00:12:55.550
You're no fun.

00:12:57.010 --> 00:12:57.590
Here you go.

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:03.300
Here you go.

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:04.890
Pudding?

00:13:04.890 --> 00:13:06.010
Pretty important, right?

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:08.600
Yeah, pudding is important.

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:14.360
Oh, it's...

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:15.730
G3=senpai!

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:17.530
Fancy meeting you here.

00:13:17.530 --> 00:13:18.530
Y-Yeah.

00:13:18.820 --> 00:13:22.990
I'm glad I bumped into you. I wanted to chat with you.

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:24.870
Me too.

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:30.790
Sig-chan disappeared too.

00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:32.960
We're the only ones paying?!

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:36.290
Damn it...

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:37.710
I wasn't planning on spending that much.

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:40.510
I don't have any allowance left.

00:13:40.510 --> 00:13:43.380
That's because you bought tons of peaches.

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:46.800
I'm going to make sure I get a return on my investment.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:50.060
A single man, living alone...

00:13:50.060 --> 00:13:53.810
I'm sure we'll find something juicy if we snoop around a little.

00:13:53.980 --> 00:13:55.520
We're just visiting him.

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:57.190
To see how he's doing, remember?

00:13:58.070 --> 00:13:58.780
I'm totally gonna use that to get my money back...

00:13:58.780 --> 00:14:00.360
<i>I wonder if taking Sixteen was a good idea after all...</i>
I'm totally gonna use that to get my money back...

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:01.900
<i>I wonder if taking Sixteen was a good idea after all...</i>

00:14:06.410 --> 00:14:08.080
Oh, Professor!

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:10.540
Good morning!

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:12.750
Who is this?

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:15.210
You don't know, Fukko?

00:14:15.210 --> 00:14:17.710
He's been here since our school was founded.

00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:19.960
Since the school was founded?!

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:20.710
Um...

00:14:21.010 --> 00:14:22.800
That means he's about thirty.

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:24.010
That old?!

00:14:24.010 --> 00:14:26.930
He'd be over 130 in people years.

00:14:26.930 --> 00:14:28.550
He's almost like a forked-dog.

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:30.060
I've heard of forked-cats, but forked-dogs?

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:36.980
Yeah, right.

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:39.440
You sure like dogs, don't you, Sixteen-chan?

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:39.610
I'm going on ahead.

00:14:39.610 --> 00:14:40.690
Good boy!
I'm going on ahead.

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:46.110
Professor, your little eyebrows are so cute...

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:49.120
There's no name plate...

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:51.080
This is it, right?

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:53.160
Go home.

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:55.540
How did you know I was here?

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:57.080
That tickles...
How did you know I was here?

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:58.750
How did you know I was here?

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:02.880
I think anyone would notice people making that much noise.

00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:04.470
True.

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:11.930
<i>But that means he knows the sound of our voices...</i>

00:15:14.310 --> 00:15:16.100
Now, go home.

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:19.690
But I brought all this for you.

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:20.610
Bye, Professor!
But I brought all this for you.

00:15:20.610 --> 00:15:21.730
Bye, Professor!

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:27.160
Damn, it's cold!

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:31.830
Hey. How's he doing?

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:36.410
Man, it's stuffy in here.

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:38.370
I think it needs some ventilation.

00:15:46.220 --> 00:15:47.260
Suspicious.

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:49.680
There must be a porn mag in here...

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:51.930
Stop it.

00:15:52.810 --> 00:15:54.810
All right! I found one!

00:15:54.810 --> 00:15:56.270
Sixteen-chan!

00:15:56.640 --> 00:16:01.310
I see. Sensei likes girls with big boobs.

00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:03.190
Take a look, Fukko.

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:05.440
"You can do whatever you want to me."

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:07.070
No, Sixteen-chan!

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:08.570
You can't just mess with that!

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:10.870
I wonder if there's anything else fun around here.

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:16.910
Oh, no! It broke!

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:19.500
That's dangerous, Sixteen-chan!

00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:22.040
The pudding fell...

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:26.510
Don't rub against it, Sixteen-chan!

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:30.130
Here's the forbidden closet!

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:31.930
Ah! SOS!

00:16:31.930 --> 00:16:33.350
Save me, Fukko!

00:16:33.350 --> 00:16:36.100
The room's getting all messed up!

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:38.020
You guys...

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:40.600
Get out!

00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:50.200
Happy new year.

00:16:50.660 --> 00:16:52.200
Let's have fun again this year.

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:56.370
Happy new year, everyone!

00:16:57.950 --> 00:17:00.160
Can't have New Year's without these.

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:02.960
You can tell what a person's like by reading these.

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:08.010
Oh, it's from the Japanese teacher.

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:10.090
What the hell?

00:17:10.970 --> 00:17:12.680
You'd think he'd write more.

00:17:13.140 --> 00:17:15.970
We're his cute little students, you know?

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:18.520
Definitely lacking in creativity.

00:17:18.520 --> 00:17:19.810
What?

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:21.690
He didn't send me one.

00:17:22.230 --> 00:17:25.820
Maybe it's because of what you did. Remember?

00:17:25.820 --> 00:17:26.730
Huh?

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:28.360
Hey, Sixteen!

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:29.740
I was just kidding.

00:17:29.740 --> 00:17:31.700
I'll be back!

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:33.950
Huh?

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:42.620
<i>Well, I might have been a little responsible...</i>

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:45.380
<i>But...</i>

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:49.590
<i>I think it's wrong to discriminate.</i>

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:52.180
<i>I'm going to give him a piece of my mind.</i>

00:17:58.390 --> 00:17:59.430
Huh?

00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:03.940
He's not here?

00:18:10.490 --> 00:18:11.610
What should I do?

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:14.450
I'm already here, so...

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:16.910
Excuse me.

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:29.840
You're gonna get worse if you sleep there.

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:40.890
<i>But a human teacher might shoot us off, you know?</i>

00:18:56.200 --> 00:19:02.040
<i>Sixteen-chan just had to say something weird like that...</i>

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:07.080
Don't shoot me!

00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:25.940
Good morning.

00:19:26.980 --> 00:19:29.190
FNC? You're here again?

00:19:29.440 --> 00:19:31.400
I made some porridge.

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:34.110
You can't just eat instant noodles all the time.

00:19:34.110 --> 00:19:36.950
You shouldn't just enter someone's room without asking.

00:19:37.490 --> 00:19:41.830
But we just took off and left things a mess last time.

00:19:41.830 --> 00:19:42.700
Yeah, but...

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:51.090
You guys are guns, aren't you?

00:19:51.090 --> 00:19:53.210
Aren't water and moisture bad for you?

00:19:53.750 --> 00:19:56.420
You're really out of the loop, aren't you, Sensei?

00:19:56.420 --> 00:19:58.800
We're military-grade weaponry.

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:00.390
If we were afraid of a little rain and rust,

00:20:00.390 --> 00:20:02.220
we wouldn't be able to function as assault rifles.

00:20:02.850 --> 00:20:04.520
Is that so?

00:20:04.520 --> 00:20:06.480
Yes, it is.

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:11.900
I don't know anything about you guys...

00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:13.110
Sensei...

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:19.110
<i>Sorry, but we still don't know your name...</i>

00:20:20.200 --> 00:20:22.370
Thanks. It was good.

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:27.080
Happy new year, Sensei.

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:28.210
Also, this is for you.

00:20:30.710 --> 00:20:33.290
It's New Year's Day today, isn't it?

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:36.880
In Belgium, we're still in the Christmas mood over New Year's.

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:39.930
I wanted you to at least have a taste of New Year's spirit.

00:20:39.930 --> 00:20:43.140
Thank you, but why are you worrying about me so much?

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:48.020
Isn't it kinda lonely to be by yourself on Christmas and New Year's?

00:20:49.440 --> 00:20:54.940
In Belgium, everyone goes to church on Christmas Eve, and Christmas Mass is held.

00:20:55.730 --> 00:21:00.450
The sound of the hymns they sing and the pipe organ are just wonderful.

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:04.410
Oh, but it's fine.

00:21:04.410 --> 00:21:07.620
We can continue learning more about each other over time.

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:09.250
I guess you're right.

00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:13.670
FNC.

00:21:13.670 --> 00:21:14.420
Yes?

00:21:15.340 --> 00:21:16.380
Here you go.

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:18.210
This is...

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:20.630
You've helped me out a lot,

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:23.340
so I wasn't sure what to write.

00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:29.020
Make sure you take care of your health, too.

00:21:29.770 --> 00:21:30.890
You wear a thong, after all.

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:38.480
<i>A thong.</i>

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:39.650
<i>Tho—</i>

00:21:41.030 --> 00:21:42.700
Funko-chan!

00:21:42.700 --> 00:21:44.030
Fukko!

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:45.570
Japanese Teacher!

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:47.830
Idiot!

00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:51.910
Again?

00:21:53.580 --> 00:22:00.210
Let's tear another page off our calendar

00:22:01.220 --> 00:22:07.720
Together we braved

00:22:12.180 --> 00:22:19.690
past ages and never-ending conflict

00:22:19.940 --> 00:22:27.320
Together we laughed and cried in those hectic times

00:22:28.160 --> 00:22:32.910
When I ran

00:22:35.830 --> 00:22:46.340
I put my footsteps into the ground

00:22:47.390 --> 00:22:54.060
Let's tear another page off our calendar

00:22:55.020 --> 00:23:01.230
Something is bound to change

00:23:02.650 --> 00:23:09.370
One by one the days I tore off pile up

00:23:09.910 --> 00:23:13.290
like a past I cannot erase

00:23:13.750 --> 00:23:19.460
They will be my strength for days to come

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:26.130
I didn't even hit him!

00:23:26.130 --> 00:23:28.800
He just fell out of the window on his own!

00:23:32.010 --> 00:23:33.270
It's time for the school fair!

00:23:33.270 --> 00:23:36.100
But it's a bit different than other school fairs you'll see!

00:23:36.100 --> 00:23:37.310
You'll be surprised!

00:23:37.310 --> 00:23:38.100
Next time:

00:23:38.100 --> 00:23:38.730
Take a look!

00:23:38.730 --> 00:23:39.360
Scold someone!

00:23:39.360 --> 00:23:40.520
Remember it!
